.TH APT-MAN 1 "October 2025" "apt-man 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apt-man \- manage APT sources, PPAs, and GPG keys with ease
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt-man
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apt-man
is a comprehensive tool for managing APT package sources, including Ubuntu PPAs,
third-party repositories, and their GPG signing keys. It supports both legacy
.list format and modern DEB822 .sources format.

The tool provides functionality to list, enable, disable, and upgrade sources,
as well as manage their associated GPG keys. It helps identify security issues
like missing keys or outdated key formats.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Source Management Commands"
.TP
.B list [\-\-keys]
List all APT sources. If \fB\-\-keys\fR is specified, also show the GPG signing
key associated with each source.
.TP
.B list \fIID\fR
Show all installed packages from the source identified by \fIID\fR.
.TP
.B list \fIID\fR \-\-available
Show all available packages in the source identified by \fIID\fR.
.TP
.B remove \fIID\fR
Remove all packages installed from the source identified by \fIID\fR.
.TP
.B disable \fIID\fR
Disable a source by renaming it with a .disabled extension. The source will
no longer be used by APT but can be re-enabled later.
.TP
.B enable \fIID\fR
Enable a previously disabled source by removing the .disabled extension.
.TP
.B list-disabled
List all disabled sources.
.TP
.B upgrade-source \fIOLD\fR \fINEW\fR
Upgrade all APT sources from OLD release codename to NEW release codename.
For example, to upgrade from "noble" to "oracular".
.TP
.B lint
Comprehensive security audit of all sources and keys. Performs 17 different
security checks including key validation, source configuration, and file permissions.
.TP
.B lint \-\-fix
Interactively fix security warnings found by the audit. This command:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Scans for HTTP sources and tests if HTTPS is available
.IP \(bu 2
Moves legacy keys to modern locations (removes old keys after backup)
.IP \(bu 2
Automatically updates .sources files with new key paths
.IP \(bu 2
Detects unreachable sources and offers to disable or remove them
.IP \(bu 2
Prompts for confirmation before each change
.IP \(bu 2
Creates timestamped backup directory with MANIFEST.txt tracking file
.IP \(bu 2
Provides clear instructions for manual steps
.RE
.IP
Changes are applied carefully to avoid breaking your APT configuration.
All backups and a manifest file are saved in /tmp/apt-man-backup-* for recovery.
.TP
.B revert [\fINUMBER\fR|\fIPATH\fR]
Revert changes made by \fBlint --fix\fR using the manifest file. Without arguments,
lists all available backups with timestamps and change counts. With a number, reverts
that backup (1 is most recent). With a path, reverts that specific backup directory.
The manifest tracks all changes (HTTP/HTTPS conversions, key moves, source
disable/remove) and reverts them in the correct order.

.SS "Security Fix Commands"
.TP
.B migrate \fIID\fR
Convert a legacy .list file to modern .sources (DEB822) format. Currently shows
manual steps for migration.
.TP
.B use-https \fIID\fR
Convert an HTTP source to HTTPS. Tests URL reachability before applying changes
and creates a backup file.

.SS "Key Management Commands"
.TP
.B keys [\-\-list]
List all GPG keys on the system, showing their format (old vs new) and location.
This is the default action when no option is specified.
.TP
.B keys \-\-check
Check all sources for missing or problematic GPG keys. Reports missing key files,
unreadable keys, and sources without keys (security risk).
.TP
.B keys \-\-refresh
Refresh GPG keys from keyservers to get updates, revocations, or new signatures.
Only affects keys in /etc/apt/keyrings/. System keyrings are updated via APT packages.
.TP
.B keys \-\-info \fIKEYFILE\fR
Show detailed information about a specific GPG key file, including key ID,
algorithm, creation date, expiration date, and status.
.TP
.B keys \-\-move \fIKEYFILE\fR
Move a legacy key from /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/ to the modern location
/etc/apt/keyrings/. Creates a backup in /tmp/, copies the key to the new
location, automatically updates all .sources files that reference the old
key path, and removes the key from the legacy location.
.TP
.B keys \-\-renewal
Show all GPG keys that will expire in the next 90 days, helping plan for
key renewals before they cause APT failures.

.SS "General Options"
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-V
Display version information and exit.

.SH KEY FORMATS
.B apt-man
recognizes and categorizes GPG keys by their format and location:

.TP
.B "OLD (deprecated)"
The legacy /etc/apt/trusted.gpg file. This format is deprecated and should
not be used for new keys.
.TP
.B "OLD (trusted.gpg.d)"
Legacy keys in /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/. These are automatically trusted by
APT but should be migrated to the new format.
.TP
.B "NEW (apt keyring)"
Modern format keys in /etc/apt/keyrings/. This is the recommended location
for user-managed keys. Sources must explicitly reference these keys.
.TP
.B "NEW (system keyring)"
System-managed keys in /usr/share/keyrings/. These are installed and updated
via APT packages.
.TP
.B "INLINE (embedded key)"
PGP keys embedded directly in DEB822 .sources files. Cannot be refreshed
from keyservers.

.SH SOURCE FORMATS
.B apt-man
supports both APT source formats:

.TP
.B ".list files"
Legacy one-line-per-source format. Keys are implicitly trusted from the
default keyring.
.TP
.B ".sources files"
Modern DEB822 format with structured fields. Supports explicit key references
via Signed-By field and inline PGP keys.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B apt-man list
List all active and disabled sources.
.TP
.B apt-man list \-\-keys
List all sources with their GPG signing keys.
.TP
.B apt-man list 2
Show installed packages from source ID 2.
.TP
.B apt-man list 2 \-\-available
Show available packages in source ID 2.
.TP
.B apt-man disable 5
Disable the source with ID 5.
.TP
.B apt-man lint
Run comprehensive security audit with 17 checks.
.TP
.B apt-man lint \-\-fix
Interactively fix security warnings with confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B apt-man revert
List all available backups from previous lint --fix sessions.
.TP
.B apt-man revert 1
Revert the most recent lint --fix changes.
.TP
.B apt-man migrate 3
Convert source ID 3 from .list to .sources format.
.TP
.B apt-man use-https 7
Convert source ID 7 from HTTP to HTTPS.
.TP
.B apt-man keys \-\-check
Check all sources for missing or problematic keys.
.TP
.B apt-man keys \-\-renewal
Show keys expiring in the next 90 days.
.TP
.B apt-man keys \-\-move /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/old.gpg
Move legacy key to modern location.
.TP
.B apt-man keys \-\-info /etc/apt/keyrings/microsoft.gpg
Show detailed information about the Microsoft key.
.TP
.B apt-man upgrade-source noble oracular
Upgrade all sources from Ubuntu Noble to Oracular.
.TP
.B apt-man list 3
Show all installed packages from source ID 3.
.TP
.B apt-man remove 4
Remove all packages installed from source ID 4.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list
Main APT sources file (may not exist on modern systems).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.list
Legacy format source files.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
Modern DEB822 format source files.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.disabled
Disabled source files (both formats).
.TP
.I /etc/apt/trusted.gpg
Deprecated keyring file.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/*.gpg
Legacy keyring directory.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/keyrings/*.gpg
Modern user-managed keyring directory (recommended).
.TP
.I /usr/share/keyrings/*.gpg
System-managed keyring directory (package-managed).
.TP
.I /tmp/sources_index
Temporary index file used during source operations.

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.IP \(bu 2
Always verify keys before adding them to your system
.IP \(bu 2
Prefer keys in /etc/apt/keyrings/ over /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/
.IP \(bu 2
Use explicit Signed-By references in .sources files
.IP \(bu 2
Regularly check for missing or expired keys
.IP \(bu 2
Be cautious with sources that don't specify keys
.IP \(bu 2
Keep keys updated, especially for third-party repositories

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B apt-man
uses standard exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error (invalid usage, missing arguments)
.TP
.B 2
File not found or permission denied

